1
00:00:00,385 --> 00:00:03,135
(Sheldon:)Have you suffered
a recent blow to the head?

2
00:00:03,764 --> 00:00:06,054
Hey, you don't have to be so mean.

3
00:00:06,224 --> 00:00:10,144
I'm sorry. Have you suffered
a recent blow to the head?

4
00:00:12,731 --> 00:00:14,481
(Penny:)No. You just suck at teaching.

5
00:00:14,650 --> 00:00:17,860
(Sheldon:)Really? Of those two explanations,
which one seems the most likely?

6
00:00:18,028 --> 00:00:19,488
(Penny:)Oh, God.

7
00:00:19,655 --> 00:00:23,245
(Penny:)Sheldon, look, I'm trying to understand
but you're going too fast.

8
00:00:23,408 --> 00:00:27,658
(Penny:)-Can you just back up a little bit?
-All right.

9
00:00:27,871 --> 00:00:31,081
(Sheldon:)It's a warm summer evening
in ancient Greece--

10
00:00:31,249 --> 00:00:32,749
(Penny:)Not that far back.

11
00:00:32,918 --> 00:00:36,508
Okay, at what point
did you begin to feel lost?

12
00:00:36,672 --> 00:00:39,632
(Penny:)I don't know. Where were we looking up
at the night sky?

13
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:41,880
(Sheldon:)-Greece.
-Damn it.

14
00:00:42,052 --> 00:00:43,972
(Penny:)Look,
there's no need to get frustrated.

15
00:00:44,137 --> 00:00:45,887
(Sheldon:)People learn at different rates.

16
00:00:46,056 --> 00:00:50,726
(Sheldon:)Unlike objects falling in a vacuum,
which...?

17
00:00:53,021 --> 00:00:55,731
(Sheldon:)MA equals MG...?

18
00:00:56,191 --> 00:00:58,321
(Penny:)-Squared?
-No.

